-- טבלאות השכר בתוקף — the tables collection's lookups (MMS-610): for a
-- day, the amount a table the corpus holds gives a teacher, a principal or
-- a first deputy, by the table family, the seniority or complexity level,
-- and the grade. Each lookup reads the tables of the tables collection and,
-- where the collection has none for a period, the agreement that annexes
-- the table (the base agreement's signed copy for 1.12.2008, the first and
-- third parts of the 2011 framework for 1.1.2011 and 1.4.2013); every table
-- it reads is checked against what produces it in its own file.
--
-- Which table a teacher of the reform is paid by — his post, his education
-- and his seniority read onto the tables' families and rows — is the last
-- section's (MMS-555), which states the combined salary the tables give a
-- full position as this collection's claim to the root. A table here governs from the day it applies
-- until the next one the corpus holds; an update the corpus knows of and
-- does not hold the table of gives no answer (the completion agreement's
-- tables of 1.1.2012, MMS-116: `the text is missing`), and an update the
-- corpus does not record at all — a cost-of-living update under §35(ב) of
-- the base agreement, a framework rise published only in a circular — is
-- not seen. The seniority is the label the table prints: the tables of
-- 1.12.2008 print 0 to 36, every later one 1 to 36; how a teacher's
-- seniority for pay maps onto a label is the rules', not the tables'.
--
-- Not read here: the BA and MA salary tables of 1.9.2022 printed to the
-- shekel (`2022-09-01_ofek-hadash_salary-table_BA`, `_MA`), which the
-- follow-up committee's decision of 14.1.2025 replaced from the same day by
-- tables printed to the agora — the whole grades of the conversion tables
-- read here (`nispach-alef-3`, `-4` assert it); and the same for their Ofek
-- 2022 supplements. The upper-division tables of the old track
-- (`nispach-alef_2008` …) are owners' circular תשע"ט/7's, whose own
-- `combined salary` reads them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `base-agreement-46`
IMPORT `tables-common`
IMPORT `2008-12-25_ofek-hadash_base-agreement_signed-registry-copy-with-annex-tables`
IMPORT `2013-04-15_ofek-hadash_tosefet-2011-third-part_tables`
IMPORT `2015-01-01_ofek-hadash_salary-tables_morim`
IMPORT `hamara-conversion-tables`
IMPORT `sachar-morim-kayamim_ma-exact`
IMPORT `sachar-morim-kayamim-a`
IMPORT `sachar-morim-kayamim-b`
IMPORT `sachar-morim-kayamim-c`
IMPORT `nispach-alef-3`
IMPORT `nispach-alef-4`
IMPORT `nispach-alef-5`
IMPORT `nispach-alef-6`
IMPORT `nispach-alef-7`
IMPORT `nispach-bet-3-gimel-3`
IMPORT `nispach-bet-4-gimel-4`
IMPORT `nispach-bet-5-gimel-5`
IMPORT `nispach-bet-6-gimel-6`
IMPORT `nispach-bet-7-gimel-7`
IMPORT `menahalim-kayamim`
IMPORT `menahalei-chativa-tzmuda-kayamim`
IMPORT `sganim-rishonim-kayamim`
IMPORT `nispach-alef-8`
IMPORT `nispach-alef-9`

§ `טבלאות השכר בתוקף`

§§ `טבלאות המורים`

@desc A family of the reform's teachers' tables: the conversion tables, by the rating code their titles print, which hold the salary tables' cells and the intermediate grades.
DECLARE `teachers' table family` IS ONE OF
    `the first-degree tables (rating 101)`
    `the second-degree tables (rating 102)`
    `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)`
    `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)`
    `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)`

-- The tables of 1.12.2008 by family: the base agreement's annexes ו' and ז'
-- (the first- and second-degree tables with intermediate grades) and ט',
-- י' and י"א (the non-academic teachers' of the three ranks), as its signed
-- copy prints them.
GIVEN f IS A `teachers' table family`
GIVETH AN `annexed pay table`
DECIDE `the teachers' table of 1.12.2008 for` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` THEN `this copy's annex ו'`
    WHEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` THEN `this copy's annex ז'`
    WHEN `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)` THEN `this copy's annex ט'`
    WHEN `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)` THEN `this copy's annex י'`
    WHEN `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)` THEN `this copy's annex י"א`

GIVEN f IS A `teachers' table family`
GIVETH A `salary table`
DECIDE `the teachers' table of 1.1.2011 for` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` THEN `annex א3'`
    WHEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` THEN `annex א4'`
    WHEN `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)` THEN `annex א5'`
    WHEN `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)` THEN `annex א6'`
    WHEN `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)` THEN `annex א7'`

GIVEN f IS A `teachers' table family`
GIVETH A `salary table`
DECIDE `the teachers' table of 1.4.2013 for` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` THEN `third-part annex א'3`
    WHEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` THEN `third-part annex א'4`
    WHEN `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)` THEN `third-part annex א'5`
    WHEN `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)` THEN `third-part annex א'6`
    WHEN `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)` THEN `third-part annex א'7`

GIVEN f IS A `teachers' table family`
GIVETH A `published table`
DECIDE `the teachers' table of 1.1.2015 for` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` THEN `annex א'3 of 1.1.2015`
    WHEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` THEN `annex א'4 of 1.1.2015`
    WHEN `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)` THEN `annex א'5 of 1.1.2015`
    WHEN `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)` THEN `annex א'6 of 1.1.2015`
    WHEN `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)` THEN `annex א'7 of 1.1.2015`

GIVEN f IS A `teachers' table family`
GIVETH A `published table`
DECIDE `the teachers' table of 1.9.2016 for` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` THEN `annex א'3 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` THEN `annex א'4 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)` THEN `annex א'5 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)` THEN `annex א'6 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)` THEN `annex א'7 of 1.9.2016`

GIVEN f IS A `teachers' table family`
GIVETH A `published table`
DECIDE `the teachers' table of 1.9.2022 for` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` THEN `annex א'3 of 1.9.2022`
    WHEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` THEN `annex א'4 of 1.9.2022`
    WHEN `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)` THEN `annex א'5 of 1.9.2022`
    WHEN `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)` THEN `annex א'6 of 1.9.2022`
    WHEN `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)` THEN `annex א'7 of 1.9.2022`

`the teachers' tables of 1.1.2015 apply from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2015
`the teachers' tables of 1.9.2016 apply from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016
`the teachers' tables of 1.9.2022 apply from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022

#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD (`the teachers' table of 1.1.2015 for` f)'s `published table from` EQUALS `the teachers' tables of 1.1.2015 apply from`) `the teachers' table families`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD (`the teachers' table of 1.9.2016 for` f)'s `published table from` EQUALS `the teachers' tables of 1.9.2016 apply from`) `the teachers' table families`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD (`the teachers' table of 1.9.2022 for` f)'s `published table from` EQUALS `the teachers' tables of 1.9.2022 apply from`) `the teachers' table families`
#ASSERT `the annexed tables are updated from` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011
#ASSERT `the annexed salary tables are updated from` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008

`the teachers' table families` MEANS
    LIST `the first-degree tables (rating 101)`, `the second-degree tables (rating 102)`, `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)`,
         `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)`, `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)`

-- The day a period's tables apply from, and the source the lookup reads
-- for it, newest first. The completion agreement's tables of 1.1.2012
-- (4% over the tables before 1.1.2011, its §92(א)(1)) are not in the
-- corpus: the period gives no answer.
@desc The table the corpus holds for a day, named by the document that publishes it.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the teachers' tables in force on` d IS
    BRANCH
        IF d `is on or after` `the teachers' tables of 1.9.2022 apply from` THEN "nispach-alef-3 … nispach-alef-7 (1.9.2022)"
        IF d `is on or after` `the teachers' tables of 1.9.2016 apply from` THEN "hamara-conversion-tables, sachar-morim-kayamim (1.9.2016)"
        IF d `is on or after` `the teachers' tables of 1.1.2015 apply from` THEN "2015-01-01_ofek-hadash_salary-tables_morim (1.1.2015)"
        IF d `is on or after` `the third part's tables are updated from` THEN "2013-04-15_ofek-hadash_tosefet-2011-third-part_tables (1.4.2013)"
        IF d `is on or after` `1 January 2012` THEN "the completion agreement's tables of 1.1.2012 — not in the corpus"
        IF d `is on or after` `the annexed tables are updated from` THEN "2011-01-25_ofek-hadash_tosefet-2011-first-part_tables (1.1.2011)"
        IF d `is on or after` `the annexed salary tables are updated from` THEN "2008-12-25_ofek-hadash_base-agreement_signed-registry-copy-with-annex-tables (1.12.2008)"
        OTHERWISE "none: the reform's tables start on 1.12.2008"

@export The monthly combined salary of a full position in the Ofek Hadash reform's teachers' tables on a day, by table family, seniority and grade
GIVEN d IS A DATE                       @desc the day the salary is for
      f IS A `teachers' table family`   @desc the rating code's family: first degree 101, second degree 102, the non-academic ranks 104 (בכיר), 105 (מוסמך), 106 (בלתי מוסמך)
      seniority IS A NUMBER             @desc the seniority for pay as the table prints it: 0–36 in the tables of 1.12.2008, 1–36 from 1.1.2011
      grade IS A NUMBER                 @desc the grade, 1 to 9, or an intermediate grade (1.5 … 8.5)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the teachers' table pay on` d f seniority grade IS
    BRANCH
        IF d `is on or after` `the teachers' tables of 1.9.2022 apply from` THEN `the published cell at` (`the teachers' table of 1.9.2022 for` f) seniority grade
        IF d `is on or after` `the teachers' tables of 1.9.2016 apply from` THEN `the published cell at` (`the teachers' table of 1.9.2016 for` f) seniority grade
        IF d `is on or after` `the teachers' tables of 1.1.2015 apply from` THEN `the published cell at` (`the teachers' table of 1.1.2015 for` f) seniority grade
        IF d `is on or after` `the third part's tables are updated from` THEN `the pay at grade` grade (`the row labelled` (`the teachers' table of 1.4.2013 for` f) seniority)
        IF d `is on or after` `1 January 2012` THEN NOTHING
        IF d `is on or after` `the annexed tables are updated from` THEN `the pay at grade` grade (`the row labelled` (`the teachers' table of 1.1.2011 for` f) seniority)
        IF d `is on or after` `the annexed salary tables are updated from` THEN `the annexed pay at` (`the teachers' table of 1.12.2008 for` f) seniority grade
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

#ASSERT `the teachers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 0 1 EQUALS JUST 5379.50
#ASSERT `the teachers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 16 1 EQUALS JUST 6874.96
#ASSERT `the teachers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 16 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the teachers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2015) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 36 9 EQUALS JUST 15999.37
#ASSERT `the teachers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 36 9 EQUALS JUST 15561.06
#ASSERT `the teachers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 3 1 EQUALS JUST 6554.52
#ASSERT `the teachers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` 36 9 EQUALS JUST 17730.40
#ASSERT `the teachers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2008) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the teachers' tables in force on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) EQUALS "the completion agreement's tables of 1.1.2012 — not in the corpus"
-- From 1.9.2022 the BA table is the decision of 14.1.2025's, to the agora.
#ASSERT `the teachers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 3 1 EQUALS `the table salary under §4 as the decision of 14.1.2025 corrects it` 1 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) 1 3 1

§§ `תוספת אופק 2022`

-- The Ofek 2022 supplement of a full position by family and grade: annexes
-- ב'3–ב'7 from 1.9.2022 (§5.1), ג'3–ג'7 from 1.9.2023 (§5.2; ג'3 too,
-- though it prints 1.1.2023 — the decision of 14.1.2025, §5). The BA and MA
-- supplements by the whole grades are these annexes' (`nispach-bet-3-gimel-3`
-- and `-4` assert the decision's agora annexes ב1, ג1, ב2, ג2 equal them).
-- Before 1.9.2022 there is no supplement table: no answer.
GIVEN f IS A `teachers' table family`
GIVETH A `published supplement`
DECIDE `the Ofek 2022 supplement of 1.9.2022 for` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` THEN `annex ב'3 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`
    WHEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` THEN `annex ב'4 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`
    WHEN `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)` THEN `annex ב'5 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`
    WHEN `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)` THEN `annex ב'6 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`
    WHEN `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)` THEN `annex ב'7 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`

GIVEN f IS A `teachers' table family`
GIVETH A `published supplement`
DECIDE `the Ofek 2022 supplement of 1.9.2023 for` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` THEN `annex ג'3 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`
    WHEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` THEN `annex ג'4 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`
    WHEN `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)` THEN `annex ג'5 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`
    WHEN `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)` THEN `annex ג'6 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`
    WHEN `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)` THEN `annex ג'7 of the Ofek 2022 supplement`

@export The monthly Ofek 2022 supplement of a full position in the Ofek Hadash reform on a day, by table family and grade
GIVEN d IS A DATE                       @desc the day the supplement is for
      f IS A `teachers' table family`   @desc the rating code's family: 101, 102, 104, 105 or 106
      grade IS A NUMBER                 @desc the grade, 1 to 9, or an intermediate grade (1.5 … 8.5)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ofek 2022 supplement table amount on` d f grade IS
    BRANCH
        IF d `is on or after` `the day annex ג3 applies from, as the decision of 14.1.2025 says` THEN `the published supplement at` (`the Ofek 2022 supplement of 1.9.2023 for` f) grade
        IF d `is on or after` DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022 THEN `the published supplement at` (`the Ofek 2022 supplement of 1.9.2022 for` f) grade
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

#ASSERT `the Ofek 2022 supplement table amount on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 1 EQUALS JUST 792.77
#ASSERT `the Ofek 2022 supplement table amount on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2023) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 1 EQUALS JUST 792.77
#ASSERT `the Ofek 2022 supplement table amount on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2023) `the first-degree tables (rating 101)` 1 EQUALS JUST 1585.54
#ASSERT `the Ofek 2022 supplement table amount on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2022) `the second-degree tables (rating 102)` 1 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `טבלאות המנהלים והסגנים`

@desc A family of the reform's principals' and first deputies' tables, by post and rank.
DECLARE `managers' table family` IS ONE OF
    `the academic principals' tables`
    `the senior-rank principals' tables`
    `the certified principals' tables`
    `the uncertified principals' tables`
    `the academic adjacent junior-high principals' tables`
    `the senior-rank adjacent junior-high principals' tables`
    `the certified adjacent junior-high principals' tables`
    `the uncertified adjacent junior-high principals' tables`
    `the academic first deputies' tables`
    `the senior-rank first deputies' tables`
    `the certified first deputies' tables`
    `the uncertified first deputies' tables`

-- From 1.1.2015: the existing principals' and deputies' tables the portal
-- prints "from 1.9.2016" (the agreement of 4.3.2015's tables raised by the
-- update of 1.1.2015, each file checks; the September 2016 agreement sets
-- no new principals' tables). A new principal's table is the existing
-- one's whole grades (`menahalim-sganim-chadashim` asserts it).
GIVEN f IS A `managers' table family`
GIVETH A `published table`
DECIDE `the managers' table of 1.1.2015 for` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the academic principals' tables` THEN `annex א'11 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the senior-rank principals' tables` THEN `annex א'12 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the certified principals' tables` THEN `annex א'13 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the uncertified principals' tables` THEN `annex א'14 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the academic adjacent junior-high principals' tables` THEN `annex א'15 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the senior-rank adjacent junior-high principals' tables` THEN `annex א'16 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the certified adjacent junior-high principals' tables` THEN `annex א'17 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the uncertified adjacent junior-high principals' tables` THEN `annex א'18 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the academic first deputies' tables` THEN `annex א'19 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the senior-rank first deputies' tables` THEN `annex א'20 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the certified first deputies' tables` THEN `annex א'21 of 1.9.2016`
    WHEN `the uncertified first deputies' tables` THEN `annex א'22 of 1.9.2016`

-- From 1.9.2022 (annex א8) and 1.9.2023 (annex א9): the academic tables
-- only — a junior-high principal in a six-year school read as the adjacent
-- junior-high principal of the earlier tables, a "deputy principal" as the
-- first deputy. A non-academic manager has no table there
-- (F-ofek-hadash-wage-2022-signed-c; the decision of 14.1.2025's annexes
-- א'8 and א'9, which add them, are not in the corpus): no answer.
GIVEN f IS A `managers' table family`, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `published table`
DECIDE `the managers' table of 2022 for` f n IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the academic adjacent junior-high principals' tables` THEN JUST (at (`the tables of 2022's annex` n) 0)
    WHEN `the academic principals' tables` THEN JUST (at (`the tables of 2022's annex` n) 1)
    WHEN `the academic first deputies' tables` THEN JUST (at (`the tables of 2022's annex` n) 2)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A LIST OF `published table`
        DECIDE `the tables of 2022's annex` k IS
            IF k EQUALS 9 THEN `the tables of annex א'9 of the principals` ELSE `the tables of annex א'8 of the principals`

@export The monthly table salary of a full position of an Ofek Hadash principal or first deputy on a day, by table family, complexity level and grade
GIVEN d IS A DATE                       @desc the day the salary is for
      f IS A `managers' table family`   @desc the post (principal, adjacent junior-high principal, first deputy) and rank (academic, senior, certified, uncertified)
      level IS A NUMBER                 @desc the school's complexity level, 1 to 8 (a deputy's from 2)
      grade IS A NUMBER                 @desc the grade: א 1, א+ 1.5, ב 2, ב+ 2.5, ג 3, ג+ 3.5, ד 4
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the managers' table pay on` d f level grade IS
    BRANCH
        IF d `is on or after` `annex א'9 of the principals is updated from` THEN
            CONSIDER `the managers' table of 2022 for` f 9
            WHEN JUST t THEN `the published cell at` t level grade
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        IF d `is on or after` `annex א'8 of the principals is updated from` THEN
            CONSIDER `the managers' table of 2022 for` f 8
            WHEN JUST t THEN `the published cell at` t level grade
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        IF d `is on or after` `the teachers' tables of 1.1.2015 apply from` THEN `the published cell at` (`the managers' table of 1.1.2015 for` f) level grade
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

#ASSERT `the managers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2015) `the academic principals' tables` 1 1 EQUALS JUST 14032.14
#ASSERT `the managers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) `the academic principals' tables` 3 2 EQUALS JUST 19643.48
#ASSERT `the managers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2023) `the academic principals' tables` 3 2 EQUALS JUST 20636.68
#ASSERT `the managers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) `the certified principals' tables` 3 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the managers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2022) `the academic first deputies' tables` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the managers' table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2014) `the academic principals' tables` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `השכר המשולב של מורה ברפורמה — מה הטבלאות אומרות לשורש`

-- The table a teacher of the reform is paid by (MMS-555). The family: a
-- first degree on the first-degree tables, a second degree on the
-- second-degree tables and a doctorate on them too (the base agreement's
-- §36(ב)–(ד)(1)); a teacher without a degree on the tables of his rank,
-- as their titles print it (בכיר 104, מוסמך 105, בלתי מוסמך 106).
GIVEN e IS A `the education the tables ask`
GIVETH A `teachers' table family`
DECIDE `the teachers' table family for` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `with a first degree`            THEN `the first-degree tables (rating 101)`
    WHEN `with a second degree`           THEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)`
    WHEN `with a doctorate`               THEN `the second-degree tables (rating 102)`
    WHEN `non-academic of senior rank`    THEN `the senior-rank tables (rating 104)`
    WHEN `non-academic of certified rank` THEN `the certified-rank tables (rating 105)`
    WHEN `non-academic and uncertified`   THEN `the uncertified-rank tables (rating 106)`

-- A principal's or first deputy's family: the post, and the rank (any
-- degree is the academic tables).
GIVEN p IS A `the post in the reform's tables`, e IS A `the education the tables ask`
GIVETH A MAYBE `managers' table family`
DECIDE `the managers' table family for` p e IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a principal in the tables` THEN
        JUST (`by rank` e `the academic principals' tables` `the senior-rank principals' tables` `the certified principals' tables` `the uncertified principals' tables`)
    WHEN `an adjacent junior-high principal in the tables` THEN
        JUST (`by rank` e `the academic adjacent junior-high principals' tables` `the senior-rank adjacent junior-high principals' tables` `the certified adjacent junior-high principals' tables` `the uncertified adjacent junior-high principals' tables`)
    WHEN `a first deputy in the tables` THEN
        JUST (`by rank` e `the academic first deputies' tables` `the senior-rank first deputies' tables` `the certified first deputies' tables` `the uncertified first deputies' tables`)
    WHEN `a teacher in the tables` THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        GIVEN x IS A `the education the tables ask`
              academic IS A `managers' table family`
              senior IS A `managers' table family`
              certified IS A `managers' table family`
              uncertified IS A `managers' table family`
        GIVETH A `managers' table family`
        DECIDE `by rank` x academic senior certified uncertified IS
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN `non-academic of senior rank`    THEN senior
            WHEN `non-academic of certified rank` THEN certified
            WHEN `non-academic and uncertified`   THEN uncertified
            OTHERWISE academic

-- The row a teacher's seniority reads (convention thresholds.seniority-row,
-- put to the lawyer): the completion agreement of 29.2.2012 (§23(א)) put
-- "בותק 1" in the place of "בותק 0" and the tables it brings start at
-- seniority 1, as every table from 1.1.2011 prints them; so a seniority
-- counted that way reads the row of its own label in those tables, and in
-- the tables of 1.12.2008, printed 0 to 36, the row one below it (a new
-- teacher, 1, at row 0). From 36 on, the last row.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, seniority IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the seniority row on` d seniority IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the annexed tables are updated from`
    THEN min 36 seniority
    ELSE min 36 (seniority MINUS 1)

#ASSERT `the seniority row on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2008) 1 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the seniority row on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011) 1 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the seniority row on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2023) 40 EQUALS 36

-- The combined salary of a full position the tables give a teacher of the
-- reform on the case's salary month: a teacher's on the teachers' tables,
-- a principal's or first deputy's on theirs.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-position table pay of` c IS
    CONSIDER `the managers' table family for` (c's `the post in the reform`) (c's `the education`)
    WHEN JUST f THEN `the managers' table pay on` (c's `the salary month`) f (c's `the school's complexity level`) (c's `the grade in the tables`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        `the teachers' table pay on` (c's `the salary month`) (`the teachers' table family for` (c's `the education`))
            (`the seniority row on` (c's `the salary month`) (c's `the seniority the tables count`)) (c's `the grade in the tables`)

-- The claim (MMS-521, MMS-555): for a teacher paid by the reform's tables,
-- the cell of the table in force. Of no one else do the tables speak.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-position combined salary according to the Ofek Hadash tables` c IS
    IF c's `paid by the Ofek Hadash tables` THEN `the full-position table pay of` c ELSE NOTHING

-- Why the tables give a teacher of the reform no figure (MMS-538): the
-- period's tables are not in the corpus (the completion agreement's of
-- 1.1.2012; the non-academic principals' and deputies' from 1.9.2022, which
-- the decision of 14.1.2025 adds in annexes the corpus does not hold), a
-- period this lookup does not read yet, or no cell at that seniority and
-- grade. NOTHING where they give one, or where they do not speak.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A MAYBE `why there is no answer`
DECIDE `why the Ofek Hadash tables give no combined salary` c IS
    IF (NOT c's `paid by the Ofek Hadash tables`) OR NOT (`the full-position table pay of` c EQUALS NOTHING)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the gap`
    WHERE
        d MEANS c's `the salary month`
        `a manager` MEANS NOT (c's `the post in the reform` EQUALS `a teacher in the tables`)
        `the gap` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `a manager` AND d `is on or after` `annex א'8 of the principals is updated from`
                THEN `the text is missing` "טבלאות השכר של מנהלים וסגנים שאינם אקדמאים מ־1.9.2022 (נספחים א'8 ו־א'9 להחלטת ועדת המעקב מיום 14.1.2025)"
                IF `a manager` AND NOT d `is on or after` `the teachers' tables of 1.1.2015 apply from`
                THEN `not yet encoded` "טבלאות השכר של המנהלים והסגנים הראשונים שלפני 1.1.2015"
                IF `a manager` THEN `the text is missing` "התא בטבלה שבתוקף ברמת המורכבות ובדרגה האלה (אין כזה, או שהקורפוס קורא אותו [לא קריא])"
                IF NOT d `is on or after` `the annexed salary tables are updated from`
                THEN `not yet encoded` "טבלאות השכר של הרפורמה שלפני 1.12.2008"
                IF d `is on or after` `1 January 2012` AND NOT d `is on or after` `the third part's tables are updated from`
                THEN `the text is missing` "טבלאות השכר של הסכם ההשלמה מיום 1.1.2012 (MMS-116)"
                OTHERWISE `the text is missing` "התא בטבלה שבתוקף בוותק ובדרגה האלה (אין כזה, או שהקורפוס קורא אותו [לא קריא])"

-- How the tables describe themselves as an instrument (MMS-521): the
-- annexes of the reform's collective agreements, from the base agreement
-- of 25.12.2008 on, as this collection reads them.
`the Ofek Hadash salary tables` MEANS
    `instrument` WITH
        `module`        IS "tables-in-force-common"
        `title`         IS "טבלאות השכר של אופק חדש (נספחי ההסכמים)"
        `kind`          IS `a collective agreement`
        `is the takanon` IS FALSE
        `issued`        IS DATE_FROM_DMY 25 12 2008
        `practised for all state employees` IS FALSE
        `approved by the Finance Minister`  IS FALSE
